§ `Fixtures -- bodies`

GIVEN `a public Act body` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `is a Town Council` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `listed in` IS A ScheduleListing,
      `regulates a profession` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `represents the community` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BodyFacts
DECIDE `a body` `a public Act body` `is a Town Council` `listed in` `regulates a profession` `represents the community` IS
    BodyFacts WITH
        `a body corporate established by a public Act for the purposes of a public function` IS `a public Act body`
        `a Town Council established under section 4 of the Town Councils Act 1988` IS `is a Town Council`
        `listed in` IS `listed in`
        `its main function is to regulate the practice and standards of a profession` IS `regulates a profession`
        `its main function is to represent particular community interests or the volunteer movement` IS `represents the community`

`a Group 1A statutory board` MEANS `a body` TRUE FALSE `Part 1 of the First Schedule` FALSE FALSE
`the Defence Science and Technology Agency` MEANS `a body` TRUE FALSE `Part 2 of the First Schedule` FALSE FALSE
`the People's Association` MEANS `a body` TRUE FALSE `Part 3 of the First Schedule` FALSE FALSE
`a Group 2A professional regulator` MEANS `a body` TRUE FALSE `Part 1 of the Second Schedule` TRUE FALSE
`a Group 2B professional regulator` MEANS `a body` TRUE FALSE `Part 2 of the Second Schedule` TRUE FALSE
`a body in Part 1 of the Second Schedule that no longer regulates a profession` MEANS `a body` TRUE FALSE `Part 1 of the Second Schedule` FALSE FALSE
`a Group 3A body representing the community` MEANS `a body` TRUE FALSE `Part 1 of the Third Schedule` FALSE TRUE
`a Group 3B body representing the community` MEANS `a body` TRUE FALSE `Part 2 of the Third Schedule` FALSE TRUE
`a body in the Third Schedule that does not represent community interests` MEANS `a body` TRUE FALSE `Part 1 of the Third Schedule` FALSE FALSE
`a Town Council` MEANS `a body` TRUE TRUE `no Schedule` FALSE FALSE
`a public Act body in no Schedule` MEANS `a body` TRUE FALSE `no Schedule` FALSE FALSE
`a private company` MEANS `a body` FALSE FALSE `no Schedule` FALSE FALSE

§ `Section 2(1) -- public body and its Groups`

#ASSERT `the body is a public body` `a Group 1A statutory board`
#ASSERT `the body is a public body` `a public Act body in no Schedule`
#ASSERT NOT `the body is a public body` `a Town Council`
#ASSERT NOT `the body is a public body` `a private company`

#ASSERT `the body is a Group 1A public body` `a Group 1A statutory board`
#ASSERT `the body is a Group 1B public body` `the Defence Science and Technology Agency`
#ASSERT `the body is a Group 1C public body` `the People's Association`
#ASSERT `the body is a Group 1 public body` `a Group 1A statutory board`
#ASSERT `the body is a Group 1 public body` `the Defence Science and Technology Agency`
#ASSERT `the body is a Group 1 public body` `the People's Association`
#ASSERT NOT `the body is a Group 1B public body` `a Group 1A statutory board`

#ASSERT `the body is a Group 2A public body` `a Group 2A professional regulator`
#ASSERT `the body is a Group 2B public body` `a Group 2B professional regulator`
#ASSERT `the body is a Group 2 public body` `a Group 2A professional regulator`
#ASSERT `the body is a Group 2 public body` `a Group 2B professional regulator`

-- THE MAIN-FUNCTION CONDITION. Group 2 carries it; Group 2A does not repeat it. A body in
-- Part 1 of the Second Schedule that no longer regulates a profession is a Group 2A public
-- body and is not a Group 2 public body.
#ASSERT `the body is a Group 2A public body` `a body in Part 1 of the Second Schedule that no longer regulates a profession`
#ASSERT NOT `the body is a Group 2 public body` `a body in Part 1 of the Second Schedule that no longer regulates a profession`
#ASSERT NOT `the body is a Group 1, 2 or 3 public body` `a body in Part 1 of the Second Schedule that no longer regulates a profession`

#ASSERT `the body is a Group 3A public body` `a Group 3A body representing the community`
#ASSERT `the body is a Group 3B public body` `a Group 3B body representing the community`
#ASSERT `the body is a Group 3 public body` `a Group 3A body representing the community`
#ASSERT `the body is a Group 3A public body` `a body in the Third Schedule that does not represent community interests`
#ASSERT NOT `the body is a Group 3 public body` `a body in the Third Schedule that does not represent community interests`

-- A public body in no Schedule is in no Group.
#ASSERT NOT `the body is a Group 1, 2 or 3 public body` `a public Act body in no Schedule`
#ASSERT NOT `the body is a Group 1, 2 or 3 public body` `a Town Council`
#ASSERT `the body is a Group 1, 2 or 3 public body` `a Group 3B body representing the community`

§ `Fixtures -- agencies and persons`

GIVEN `the body` IS A BodyFacts,
      `a ministry or department` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `is an Organ of State` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `declared by the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN AgencyFacts
DECIDE `an agency` `the body` `a ministry or department` `is an Organ of State` `declared by the Minister` IS
    AgencyFacts WITH
        `the body` IS `the body`
        `a ministry or department of the Government` IS `a ministry or department`
        `an Organ of State` IS `is an Organ of State`
        `declared by the Minister by order in the Gazette to be a Singapore public sector agency` IS `declared by the Minister`

`a statutory board as an agency` MEANS `an agency` `a Group 1A statutory board` FALSE FALSE FALSE
`a ministry` MEANS `an agency` `a private company` TRUE FALSE FALSE
`an Organ of State` MEANS `an agency` `a private company` FALSE TRUE FALSE
`a body the Minister has declared an agency` MEANS `an agency` `a private company` FALSE FALSE TRUE
`a Town Council the Minister has not declared` MEANS `an agency` `a Town Council` FALSE FALSE FALSE
`a Town Council the Minister has declared` MEANS `an agency` `a Town Council` FALSE FALSE TRUE
`a Group 2A body failing the main-function test` MEANS `an agency` `a body in Part 1 of the Second Schedule that no longer regulates a profession` FALSE FALSE FALSE
`an agency of no kind` MEANS `an agency` `a private company` FALSE FALSE FALSE

#ASSERT `this is a Singapore public sector agency` `a statutory board as an agency`
#ASSERT `this is a Singapore public sector agency` `a ministry`
#ASSERT `this is a Singapore public sector agency` `an Organ of State`
#ASSERT `this is a Singapore public sector agency` `a body the Minister has declared an agency`
#ASSERT NOT `this is a Singapore public sector agency` `a Town Council the Minister has not declared`
#ASSERT `this is a Singapore public sector agency` `a Town Council the Minister has declared`
#ASSERT NOT `this is a Singapore public sector agency` `a Group 2A body failing the main-function test`
#ASSERT NOT `this is a Singapore public sector agency` `an agency of no kind`

GIVEN `a public officer` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `an employee` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `a secondee` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `a member` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the chief executive` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `a contractor` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `a contractor's employee` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `at the time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A PersonFacts
DECIDE `a person` `a public officer` `an employee` `a secondee` `a member` `the chief executive` `a contractor` `a contractor's employee` `at the time` IS
    PersonFacts WITH
        `a public officer holding a post in the ministry, department or Organ of State, including on leave without pay` IS `a public officer`
        `an employee of the Group 1, 2 or 3 public body, including on leave without pay` IS `an employee`
        `under a secondment arrangement making the individual's service available to the agency` IS `a secondee`
        `a member of the public body or of its governing body` IS `a member`
        `the chief executive of the public body` IS `the chief executive`
        `a contractor supplying goods or services to the agency or to another agency` IS `a contractor`
        `an employee of such a contractor` IS `a contractor's employee`
        `at the time of the conduct` IS `at the time`

`a civil servant, including one on leave without pay` MEANS `a person` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE
`an employee of the statutory board` MEANS `a person` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE
`a secondee to the agency` MEANS `a person` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE
`a member of the board` MEANS `a person` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE
`the chief executive of the board` MEANS `a person` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE
`a contractor to the agency` MEANS `a person` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE
`an employee of a contractor to the agency` MEANS `a person` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE
`a former employee of the statutory board` MEANS `a person` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`a stranger` MEANS `a person` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE

§ `Section 2(2) and 7(7) -- officers and relevant public officials`

#ASSERT `the person is an officer of the agency` `a civil servant, including one on leave without pay`
#ASSERT `the person is an officer of the agency` `an employee of the statutory board`
#ASSERT `the person is an officer of the agency` `a secondee to the agency`

-- Members and chief executives are relevant public officials without being "officers" in the
-- s 2(2) sense.
#ASSERT NOT `the person is an officer of the agency` `a member of the board`
#ASSERT `the person is a relevant public official` `a member of the board`
#ASSERT `the person is a relevant public official` `the chief executive of the board`
#ASSERT `the person is a relevant public official` `a civil servant, including one on leave without pay`
#ASSERT `the person is a relevant public official` `a secondee to the agency`

-- A contractor and a contractor's employee are not.
#ASSERT NOT `the person is a relevant public official` `a contractor to the agency`
#ASSERT NOT `the person is a relevant public official` `an employee of a contractor to the agency`
#ASSERT NOT `the person is a relevant public official` `a stranger`

-- "At the time of the disclosure": a person who has left is not, however recently.
#ASSERT NOT `the person is a relevant public official` `a former employee of the statutory board`
#ASSERT NOT `the person is an officer of the agency` `a former employee of the statutory board`

-- s 2(3): control.
#ASSERT `the information is under the agency's control` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `the information is under the agency's control` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the information is under the agency's control` FALSE FALSE

§ `Section 4 -- the power to direct`

#ASSERT `section 4 empowers the direction` `a sound direction on data governance for efficiency`
#ASSERT `section 4 empowers the direction` `a sound direction on information technology for business continuity`
#ASSERT `section 4 empowers the direction` `a sound direction on personnel policy to uphold values`
#ASSERT `section 4 empowers the direction` `a sound direction on official documents for efficiency of programmes`
#ASSERT `section 4 empowers the direction` `a sound direction on finance for stewardship`
#ASSERT `section 4 empowers the direction` `a direction for the purpose of managing risk to the Government's finances`
#ASSERT `section 4 empowers the direction` `a direction for the purpose of a whole-of-government approach`

-- Each of the seven purposes on its own is enough; none at all is not.
#ASSERT `the direction serves one of the seven permitted purposes` `a sound direction on data governance for efficiency`
#ASSERT NOT `the direction serves one of the seven permitted purposes` `a direction with no permitted purpose`
#ASSERT NOT `section 4 empowers the direction` `a direction with no permitted purpose`

#ASSERT NOT `the subject matter is pertinent` `a direction on a subject that is not pertinent`
#ASSERT NOT `section 4 empowers the direction` `a direction on a subject that is not pertinent`
#ASSERT NOT `section 4 empowers the direction` `a direction not recommended by the relevant Minister`
#ASSERT NOT `section 4 empowers the direction` `a direction that does not require compliance with a Government policy`
#ASSERT NOT `section 4 empowers the direction` `a direction not given by the Minister`

-- s 11(3): a policy on dismissals is within the power, one dismissal is not.
#ASSERT `section 11(3) takes the direction outside the Minister's power` `a direction to dismiss one named officer`
#ASSERT NOT `section 4 empowers the direction` `a direction to dismiss one named officer`
#ASSERT `section 11(3) takes the direction outside the Minister's power` `a direction to bring about a particular result for a named person`
#ASSERT NOT `section 4 empowers the direction` `a direction to bring about a particular result for a named person`
#ASSERT NOT `section 11(3) takes the direction outside the Minister's power` `a sound direction on personnel policy to uphold values`

-- s 11(1): inconsistent with an Act.
#ASSERT NOT `section 4 empowers the direction` `a direction inconsistent with an Act`

-- s 11(2): cut back, not struck down.
#ASSERT `the direction binds the agency in full` `a sound direction on data governance for efficiency`
#ASSERT NOT `the direction binds the agency in part` `a sound direction on data governance for efficiency`
#ASSERT `section 4 empowers the direction` `a direction that would impede a statutorily independent function`
#ASSERT `the direction binds the agency in part` `a direction that would impede a statutorily independent function`
#ASSERT NOT `the direction binds the agency in full` `a direction that would impede a statutorily independent function`
#ASSERT `the direction binds the agency in part` `a direction that would impede a quasi-judicial function`
#ASSERT NOT `the direction binds the agency in part` `a direction inconsistent with an Act`

-- s 4(4): the relevant Minister for each pertinent subject matter.
#ASSERT `the relevant Minister for the subject matter` `employment, management and discipline of employees` EQUALS `the Minister responsible for public sector personnel policy`
#ASSERT `the relevant Minister for the subject matter` `management of official documents` EQUALS `the Minister responsible for Government records and archives`
#ASSERT `the relevant Minister for the subject matter` `financial and resource management and accountability` EQUALS `the Minister responsible for Government finance`
#ASSERT `the relevant Minister for the subject matter` `use or development of information technology` EQUALS `the Minister responsible for public sector information-communications technology and related engineering`
#ASSERT `the relevant Minister for the subject matter` `data governance and sharing of information between agencies` EQUALS `the Minister responsible for public sector data governance`
#ASSERT `the relevant Minister for the subject matter` `something else` EQUALS `no relevant Minister`

§ `Section 5 -- directions by the responsible Minister`

#ASSERT `a section 5 direction may be given to the body` `a Group 1A statutory board` TRUE
#ASSERT `a section 5 direction may be given to the body` `the Defence Science and Technology Agency` TRUE
#ASSERT `a section 5 direction may be given to the body` `the People's Association` TRUE

-- The consultation the constitutional Act requires is preserved by s 5(2).
#ASSERT NOT `a section 5 direction may be given to the body` `a Group 1A statutory board` FALSE

-- Only Group 1. A Group 2 or Group 3 body can be given a s 4 direction and not a s 5 one.
#ASSERT NOT `a section 5 direction may be given to the body` `a Group 2A professional regulator` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `a section 5 direction may be given to the body` `a Group 3B body representing the community` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `a section 5 direction may be given to the body` `a body in Part 1 of the Second Schedule that no longer regulates a profession` TRUE

§ `Section 6 -- authority to share`

GIVEN `a data sharing direction has been given` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the sharer is the agency, an officer or a member` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the recipient is an agency` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `within the extent permitted` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the obligation` IS A ConfidentialityObligation
GIVETH A SharingFacts
DECIDE `a sharing` `a data sharing direction has been given` `the sharer is the agency, an officer or a member` `the recipient is an agency` `within the extent permitted` `the obligation` IS
    SharingFacts WITH
        `a data sharing direction has been given under section 4 to the agency` IS `a data sharing direction has been given`
        `the person sharing is the agency, one of its officers, or a member of the public body` IS `the sharer is the agency, an officer or a member`
        `the recipient is another Singapore public sector agency` IS `the recipient is an agency`
        `the sharing is within the extent the direction permits` IS `within the extent permitted`
        `the obligation standing in the way` IS `the obligation`

`sharing against a common law duty of confidence` MEANS `a sharing` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `a duty of confidence at common law`
`sharing against legal privilege` MEANS `a sharing` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `legal privilege`
`sharing against a contractual duty` MEANS `a sharing` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `a contractual obligation of confidentiality`
`sharing against a statutory secrecy provision` MEANS `a sharing` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `a statutory secrecy provision in another Act`
`sharing with no obligation in the way` MEANS `a sharing` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `no obligation at all`
`sharing with no direction` MEANS `a sharing` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE `a duty of confidence at common law`
`sharing outside the extent the direction permits` MEANS `a sharing` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE `a duty of confidence at common law`
`sharing with a recipient that is not an agency` MEANS `a sharing` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE `a duty of confidence at common law`
`sharing by someone who is not the agency, an officer or a member` MEANS `a sharing` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE `a duty of confidence at common law`

#ASSERT `section 6 authorises the sharing` `sharing against a common law duty of confidence`
#ASSERT `the obligation no longer stands in the way` `sharing against a common law duty of confidence`

-- What s 6 overrides is the common law of confidence and nothing else.
#ASSERT `section 6(1) overrides the obligation` `a duty of confidence at common law`
#ASSERT NOT `section 6(1) overrides the obligation` `legal privilege`
#ASSERT NOT `section 6(1) overrides the obligation` `a contractual obligation of confidentiality`
#ASSERT NOT `section 6(1) overrides the obligation` `a statutory secrecy provision in another Act`

-- Authorised, and yet the obstacle remains, for privilege, contract and a statutory secrecy provision.
#ASSERT `section 6 authorises the sharing` `sharing against legal privilege`
#ASSERT NOT `the obligation no longer stands in the way` `sharing against legal privilege`
#ASSERT NOT `the obligation no longer stands in the way` `sharing against a contractual duty`
#ASSERT NOT `the obligation no longer stands in the way` `sharing against a statutory secrecy provision`
#ASSERT `the obligation no longer stands in the way` `sharing with no obligation in the way`

#ASSERT NOT `section 6 authorises the sharing` `sharing with no direction`
#ASSERT NOT `section 6 authorises the sharing` `sharing outside the extent the direction permits`
#ASSERT NOT `section 6 authorises the sharing` `sharing with a recipient that is not an agency`
#ASSERT NOT `section 6 authorises the sharing` `sharing by someone who is not the agency, an officer or a member`

§ `Fixtures -- offences`

GIVEN `generally available` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `proved permitted by law` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `court order` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DefenceFacts
DECIDE `defences` `generally available` `proved permitted by law` `court order` `prescribed` IS
    DefenceFacts WITH
        `the defendant proves the information was generally available at the time` IS `generally available`
        `the defendant proves the act was permitted or required by or under an Act or other law` IS `proved permitted by law`
        `the defendant proves the act was authorised or required by an order of court` IS `court order`
        `the defendant proves the act was in circumstances or for a purpose prescribed` IS `prescribed`

`no defence` MEANS `defences` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`generally available information` MEANS `defences` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`permitted by law` MEANS `defences` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
`required by an order of court` MEANS `defences` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
`a prescribed purpose` MEANS `defences` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE

GIVEN `the person` IS A PersonFacts,
      `disclosed` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `under the agency's control` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `authorised by a direction` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `knew` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `reckless` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the defences` IS A DefenceFacts
GIVETH A DisclosureFacts
DECIDE `a disclosure` `the person` `disclosed` `under the agency's control` `authorised by a direction` `knew` `reckless` `the defences` IS
    DisclosureFacts WITH
        `the person` IS `the person`
        `disclosed information, or caused its disclosure, to another person` IS `disclosed`
        `the information is under the control of the agency` IS `under the agency's control`
        `the disclosure was authorised by a data sharing direction given to the agency` IS `authorised by a direction`
        `knew the disclosure was not in accordance with that direction` IS `knew`
        `was reckless as to whether it was in accordance with that direction` IS `reckless`
        `the defences` IS `the defences`

`an official knowingly discloses, with no defence` MEANS `a disclosure` `a civil servant, including one on leave without pay` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE `no defence`
`an official recklessly discloses` MEANS `a disclosure` `an employee of the statutory board` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE `no defence`
`a board member knowingly discloses` MEANS `a disclosure` `a member of the board` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE `no defence`
`an official discloses under a data sharing direction` MEANS `a disclosure` `a civil servant, including one on leave without pay` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE `no defence`
`an official discloses generally available information` MEANS `a disclosure` `a civil servant, including one on leave without pay` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE `generally available information`
`an official discloses as the law permits` MEANS `a disclosure` `a civil servant, including one on leave without pay` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE `permitted by law`
`an official discloses under a court order` MEANS `a disclosure` `a civil servant, including one on leave without pay` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE `required by an order of court`
`an official discloses for a prescribed purpose` MEANS `a disclosure` `a civil servant, including one on leave without pay` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE `a prescribed purpose`
`a contractor's employee knowingly discloses` MEANS `a disclosure` `an employee of a contractor to the agency` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE `no defence`
`a former employee knowingly discloses` MEANS `a disclosure` `a former employee of the statutory board` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE `no defence`
`an official discloses without knowing or being reckless` MEANS `a disclosure` `a civil servant, including one on leave without pay` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `no defence`
`an official does not disclose` MEANS `a disclosure` `a civil servant, including one on leave without pay` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE `no defence`
`an official discloses information the agency does not control` MEANS `a disclosure` `a civil servant, including one on leave without pay` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `no defence`

§ `Section 7(1) -- unauthorised disclosure`

#ASSERT `an offence under section 7(1) is committed` `an official knowingly discloses, with no defence`
#ASSERT `an offence under section 7(1) is committed` `an official recklessly discloses`
#ASSERT `an offence under section 7(1) is committed` `a board member knowingly discloses`

-- There is no requirement of gain, harm or loss. The fixtures above carry none.
#ASSERT (`an official discloses under a data sharing direction`'s `the disclosure was authorised by a data sharing direction given to the agency`)
#ASSERT NOT `an offence under section 7(1) is committed` `an official discloses under a data sharing direction`
#ASSERT NOT `an offence under section 7(1) is committed` `an official discloses without knowing or being reckless`
#ASSERT NOT `an offence under section 7(1) is committed` `an official does not disclose`
#ASSERT NOT `an offence under section 7(1) is committed` `an official discloses information the agency does not control`

-- The defences must each be PROVED by the defendant. With the elements made out and a defence
-- proved, the offence falls away; the elements are still made out.
#ASSERT `the elements of section 7(1) are made out` `an official discloses generally available information`
#ASSERT NOT `an offence under section 7(1) is committed` `an official discloses generally available information`
#ASSERT `the elements of section 7(1) are made out` `an official discloses as the law permits`
#ASSERT NOT `an offence under section 7(1) is committed` `an official discloses as the law permits`
#ASSERT NOT `an offence under section 7(1) is committed` `an official discloses under a court order`
#ASSERT NOT `an offence under section 7(1) is committed` `an official discloses for a prescribed purpose`
#ASSERT `the elements of section 7(1) are made out` `an official knowingly discloses, with no defence`

-- Only a relevant public official can commit it.
#ASSERT NOT `an offence under section 7(1) is committed` `a contractor's employee knowingly discloses`
#ASSERT NOT `an offence under section 7(1) is committed` `a former employee knowingly discloses`

-- s 7(6): a defence under this Act is not a defence under any other law.
#ASSERT NOT `a defence under section 7 is a defence under every other law`

#ASSERT `the maximum fine for the offences in sections 7 and 8, in dollars` EQUALS 5000
#ASSERT `the maximum imprisonment for the offences in sections 7 and 8, in months` EQUALS 24

§ `Section 7(3) -- unauthorised use with a result`

GIVEN `the person` IS A PersonFacts,
      `made use` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `authorised by a direction` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `knew` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `reckless` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `gain` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `harm` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `a loss to another person` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `only the loss of own personal data` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the defences` IS A DefenceFacts
GIVETH A UseFacts
DECIDE `a use` `the person` `made use` `authorised by a direction` `knew` `reckless` `gain` `harm` `a loss to another person` `only the loss of own personal data` `the defences` IS
    UseFacts WITH
        `the person` IS `the person`
        `made use of information under the control of an agency` IS `made use`
        `the use was authorised by a data sharing direction given to the agency` IS `authorised by a direction`
        `knew the use was not in accordance with such a direction` IS `knew`
        `was reckless as to whether it was in accordance with such a direction` IS `reckless`
        `obtained a gain for the individual or another person` IS `gain`
        `caused harm to another individual` IS `harm`
        `caused a loss to another person other than the loss of that person's own personal data` IS `a loss to another person`
        `the only loss caused was the loss of the individual's own personal data` IS `only the loss of own personal data`
        `the defences` IS `the defences`

`an official uses for gain` MEANS `a use` `a civil servant, including one on leave without pay` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `no defence`
`an official recklessly uses to cause harassment` MEANS `a use` `an employee of the statutory board` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `no defence`
`an official uses to cause someone a financial loss` MEANS `a use` `a member of the board` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `no defence`
`an official's misuse costs the individual only the loss of their own personal data` MEANS `a use` `a civil servant, including one on leave without pay` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE `no defence`
`an official uses but nothing follows` MEANS `a use` `a civil servant, including one on leave without pay` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `no defence`
`an official uses under a data sharing direction` MEANS `a use` `a civil servant, including one on leave without pay` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `no defence`
`an official uses for gain as the law permits` MEANS `a use` `a civil servant, including one on leave without pay` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `permitted by law`
`a contractor's employee uses government data for gain` MEANS `a use` `an employee of a contractor to the agency` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `no defence`

#ASSERT `an offence under section 7(3) is committed` `an official uses for gain`
#ASSERT `an offence under section 7(3) is committed` `an official recklessly uses to cause harassment`
#ASSERT `an offence under section 7(3) is committed` `an official uses to cause someone a financial loss`

-- THE LOSS DEFINITION. An official who misuses someone's personal data and causes them only the
-- loss of that personal data has caused no "loss" within the section.
#ASSERT NOT `a result within section 7(3)(e) followed` `an official's misuse costs the individual only the loss of their own personal data`
#ASSERT NOT `an offence under section 7(3) is committed` `an official's misuse costs the individual only the loss of their own personal data`

-- Unlike the disclosure offence, the use offence needs a result.
#ASSERT NOT `an offence under section 7(3) is committed` `an official uses but nothing follows`
#ASSERT NOT `an offence under section 7(3) is committed` `an official uses under a data sharing direction`
#ASSERT NOT `an offence under section 7(3) is committed` `an official uses for gain as the law permits`
#ASSERT NOT `an offence under section 7(3) is committed` `a contractor's employee uses government data for gain`

§ `Section 7(4) -- the contractor's offence`

GIVEN `the person` IS A PersonFacts,
      `made use` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `personal data` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `authorised by the agency` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `knew` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `reckless` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `gain` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `harm` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `a loss to another person` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the defences` IS A DefenceFacts
GIVETH A ContractorUseFacts
DECIDE `a contractor's use` `the person` `made use` `personal data` `authorised by the agency` `knew` `reckless` `gain` `harm` `a loss to another person` `the defences` IS
    ContractorUseFacts WITH
        `the person` IS `the person`
        `made use of information under the control of an agency` IS `made use`
        `the information is personal data` IS `personal data`
        `the use was authorised by the agency` IS `authorised by the agency`
        `knew the use was not authorised by the agency` IS `knew`
        `was reckless as to whether it was authorised by the agency` IS `reckless`
        `obtained a gain for the individual or another person` IS `gain`
        `caused harm to another individual` IS `harm`
        `caused a loss to another person other than the loss of that person's own personal data` IS `a loss to another person`
        `the defences` IS `the defences`

`a contractor uses non-personal data for gain` MEANS `a contractor's use` `a contractor to the agency` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `no defence`
`a contractor's employee recklessly uses non-personal data to cause harm` MEANS `a contractor's use` `an employee of a contractor to the agency` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE `no defence`
`a contractor uses PERSONAL data for gain` MEANS `a contractor's use` `a contractor to the agency` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `no defence`
`a contractor uses non-personal data with the agency's authority` MEANS `a contractor's use` `a contractor to the agency` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `no defence`
`an official uses non-personal data for gain, and is not a contractor` MEANS `a contractor's use` `a civil servant, including one on leave without pay` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `no defence`
`a contractor uses non-personal data but nothing follows` MEANS `a contractor's use` `a contractor to the agency` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `no defence`
`a contractor uses non-personal data for gain as the law permits` MEANS `a contractor's use` `a contractor to the agency` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `permitted by law`

#ASSERT `the person is a contractor or a contractor's employee within section 7(4)(c)` `a contractor to the agency`
#ASSERT `the person is a contractor or a contractor's employee within section 7(4)(c)` `an employee of a contractor to the agency`
#ASSERT NOT `the person is a contractor or a contractor's employee within section 7(4)(c)` `a civil servant, including one on leave without pay`

#ASSERT `an offence under section 7(4) is committed` `a contractor uses non-personal data for gain`
#ASSERT `an offence under section 7(4) is committed` `a contractor's employee recklessly uses non-personal data to cause harm`

-- THE EXCLUSION OF PERSONAL DATA. The contractor's offence covers "information (other than
-- personal data)". A contractor who misuses personal data commits no offence under this section.
#ASSERT NOT `an offence under section 7(4) is committed` `a contractor uses PERSONAL data for gain`

-- The authorisation tested is the agency's, not a data sharing direction.
#ASSERT NOT `an offence under section 7(4) is committed` `a contractor uses non-personal data with the agency's authority`
#ASSERT NOT `an offence under section 7(4) is committed` `an official uses non-personal data for gain, and is not a contractor`
#ASSERT NOT `an offence under section 7(4) is committed` `a contractor uses non-personal data but nothing follows`
#ASSERT NOT `an offence under section 7(4) is committed` `a contractor uses non-personal data for gain as the law permits`

-- And there is no contractor's offence of DISCLOSURE: the contractor's employee who knowingly
-- discloses commits no offence under s 7(1) either.
#ASSERT NOT `an offence under section 7(1) is committed` `a contractor's employee knowingly discloses`

§ `Section 8 -- unauthorised re-identification`

GIVEN `the person` IS A PersonFacts,
      `took action to re-identify` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `authorised by a direction` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `knew` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `reckless` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `publicly available` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `proved permitted by law` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `reasonably believed a specified purpose` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `notified as soon as practicable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A ReidentificationFacts
DECIDE `a re-identification` `the person` `took action to re-identify` `authorised by a direction` `knew` `reckless` `publicly available` `proved permitted by law` `reasonably believed a specified purpose` `notified as soon as practicable` IS
    ReidentificationFacts WITH
        `the person` IS `the person`
        `took action to re-identify, or caused re-identification of, the person to whom anonymised information relates` IS `took action to re-identify`
        `the re-identification was authorised by a data sharing direction given to the agency` IS `authorised by a direction`
        `knew the re-identification was not authorised by that direction` IS `knew`
        `was reckless as to whether it was authorised by that direction` IS `reckless`
        `the accused proves the information on the identity is publicly available` IS `publicly available`
        `the accused proves the action was permitted or required by law, authorised by court order, or in prescribed circumstances` IS `proved permitted by law`
        `the accused proves they reasonably believed the re-identification was for a specified purpose` IS `reasonably believed a specified purpose`
        `the accused proves they notified the agency or the Government Technology Agency as soon as was practicable` IS `notified as soon as practicable`

`an official knowingly re-identifies` MEANS `a re-identification` `a civil servant, including one on leave without pay` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`an official recklessly re-identifies` MEANS `a re-identification` `a member of the board` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`an official re-identifies under a data sharing direction` MEANS `a re-identification` `a civil servant, including one on leave without pay` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`an official re-identifies from publicly available information` MEANS `a re-identification` `a civil servant, including one on leave without pay` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`an official re-identifies as the law permits` MEANS `a re-identification` `a civil servant, including one on leave without pay` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
`an official reasonably believed it was for a specified purpose and notified promptly` MEANS `a re-identification` `a civil servant, including one on leave without pay` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE
`an official reasonably believed it was for a specified purpose and did not notify` MEANS `a re-identification` `a civil servant, including one on leave without pay` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
`an official notified promptly but had no reasonable belief` MEANS `a re-identification` `a civil servant, including one on leave without pay` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE
`a contractor's employee re-identifies` MEANS `a re-identification` `an employee of a contractor to the agency` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE

#ASSERT `an offence under section 8(1) is committed` `an official knowingly re-identifies`
#ASSERT `an offence under section 8(1) is committed` `an official recklessly re-identifies`
#ASSERT NOT `an offence under section 8(1) is committed` `an official re-identifies under a data sharing direction`
#ASSERT NOT `an offence under section 8(1) is committed` `an official re-identifies from publicly available information`
#ASSERT NOT `an offence under section 8(1) is committed` `an official re-identifies as the law permits`

-- Defence (c) needs BOTH halves.
#ASSERT NOT `an offence under section 8(1) is committed` `an official reasonably believed it was for a specified purpose and notified promptly`
#ASSERT `an offence under section 8(1) is committed` `an official reasonably believed it was for a specified purpose and did not notify`
#ASSERT `an offence under section 8(1) is committed` `an official notified promptly but had no reasonable belief`

-- A contractor's employee is not a relevant public official, and s 8 has no contractor's limb.
#ASSERT NOT `an offence under section 8(1) is committed` `a contractor's employee re-identifies`

§ `Sections 9, 10, 11 -- the form and effect of directions`

#ASSERT NOT `a direction under section 4 or 5 has legislative effect`
#ASSERT `the agency must comply` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the agency must comply` FALSE
#ASSERT `compliance with a direction is one of the body's functions under written law` `a Group 1A statutory board`
